        {
          "page": "Page 2",
          "section": "Material and methods",
          "quote": "Under the HRS condition with a temperature gradient about 2-6 K mm-1, the seed was plugged into the mold from the opening bottom in a modified Bridgman furnace for directional solidification experiments. During directional solidification, the furnace chamber was evacuated to a partial pressure of approximately 2 10-2 Pa, and the ceramic mold with seed was preheated to 1550 C for 10-20 min. Next, the DD3 ingot was melted at 1500 C and poured into the preheated mold cavity, holding for 15-20 min to stabilize. After that, the sample was pulled out at a pre-determined rate of 100 mm s-1 and was finally removed from the casting body.",
